WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:02.767
(bright music)

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:12.405
- [Wayne] Thank you very much.

00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:15.322
(Catherine laughs)

00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:20.368
- I'm Catherine, and
this is my husband Wayne.

00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:23.785
- I'm Wayne, and welcome to Freedom Cove.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.696
We live in a secluded cove.

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:30.160
The only options we have
to get here is by water.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.685
There are no road accesses.

00:00:32.685 --> 00:00:34.768
The water is our highway.

00:00:37.464 --> 00:00:39.832
- [Catherine] Everything that you see here

00:00:39.832 --> 00:00:41.832
in our home is floating.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.016
We are tied to shore with lines.

00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:46.683
We are not anchored.

00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:50.904
We have our main living house,

00:00:50.904 --> 00:00:54.936
we have the dance floor,
the lighthouse building,

00:00:54.936 --> 00:00:56.856
four greenhouses.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.472
As I started to grow the
garden and make it larger,

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:05.154
then we had to have more
space for that garden.

00:01:05.154 --> 00:01:07.640
- Everything's done with
a handsaw and hammer.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.534
No power tools.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.787
I know every board and nail by name.

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:12.454
It's about 500 tons.

00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:16.120
A million pounds that I'm floating.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.675
I've been building tree
forts since I was seven.

00:01:18.675 --> 00:01:19.508
And I said, "Well, Dad,

00:01:19.508 --> 00:01:21.133
"I'm putting a tree fort in the ocean."

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:25.357
No, when I go to town I get landsick.

00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:26.190
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:30.636
- The thing about living
in Clayoquot Sound

00:01:30.636 --> 00:01:33.347
on the west coast of Vancouver Island is

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:35.200
it's the richest biomass on Earth,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.552
so the opportunity to
fish for dinner is big.

00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:40.472
I just get in my canoe and paddle out,

00:01:40.472 --> 00:01:43.222
in 10 minutes I can catch a fish.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.360
But when it's windy and
too rough out there,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.248
I can lay on the couch
and fish out of the house.

00:01:50.248 --> 00:01:53.469
I was hoping to make a lot
more money as an artist,

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:56.648
so subsistence living
was our only opportunity

00:01:56.648 --> 00:01:57.937
to have anything as artists.

00:01:57.937 --> 00:01:59.165
We could never buy real estate,

00:01:59.165 --> 00:02:01.256
so we had to make our own.

00:02:01.256 --> 00:02:03.382
It was a great opportunity

00:02:03.382 --> 00:02:05.101
to actually move away from the city,

00:02:05.101 --> 00:02:08.610
to see if we could prosper out here.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.856
Now 24 years later, we're still doing it.

00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:16.109
- I can't imagine living any other way.

00:02:16.109 --> 00:02:19.160
I feel completely fulfilled.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.327
- (laughs) That's good, hon.

00:02:20.327 --> 00:02:21.552
(Catherine laughs)

00:02:21.552 --> 00:02:22.845
That's really nice.

00:02:22.845 --> 00:02:25.070
I'm working on it.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.653
(bright music)

